WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.337 --> 00:00:03.169
(swoosh)

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:04.914
- Next up is Kathleen Tate.

00:00:04.914 --> 00:00:08.369
Now Kathleen, she attended Sage Summit,

00:00:08.369 --> 00:00:10.299
she came to my session,

00:00:10.299 --> 00:00:13.775
and then when I was leaving
she drove into the airport.

00:00:13.775 --> 00:00:17.174
She's a hardcore fan from Chicago.

00:00:17.174 --> 00:00:18.007
She writes in to say,

00:00:18.007 --> 00:00:20.161
"My fear is that I'm a social worker

00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:22.293
"attempting to get into the fashion world.

00:00:22.293 --> 00:00:23.655
"I get motivation from Evan's channel

00:00:23.655 --> 00:00:26.216
"and now his book, Your One Word.

00:00:26.216 --> 00:00:29.367
"Do you have advice on moving
from a part time entrepreneur

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.667
"to a full time entrepreneur?"

00:00:31.667 --> 00:00:33.417
- Yeah, hey Kathleen.

00:00:34.366 --> 00:00:37.841
I'm sorry I didn't give
you a ride to the airport,

00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:41.174
but Evan Almighty, he rocked in Chicago.

00:00:42.256 --> 00:00:44.090
He set the Windy City alive,

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:47.173
and I think some context around that.

00:00:48.989 --> 00:00:51.320
I think we really have an opportunity.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.153
You're in search of work.

00:00:52.153 --> 00:00:55.141
Wow, what a great job you do.

00:00:55.141 --> 00:00:58.957
Without you, the world would
be just a lesser place,

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:01.374
and people who do social work

00:01:02.671 --> 00:01:04.539
should be valued by everybody,

00:01:04.539 --> 00:01:08.289
and it creates great social cohesion.

00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:10.548
We've talked before about
caring for the vulnerable,

00:01:10.548 --> 00:01:12.620
so you walk it everyday.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.056
Now I think if you want to get into things

00:01:15.056 --> 00:01:17.083
like fashion, designer fashion,

00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:18.604
actually you've got a great platform

00:01:18.604 --> 00:01:21.001
in terms of your current job.

00:01:21.001 --> 00:01:23.954
What I'd advocate you do is again,

00:01:23.954 --> 00:01:26.518
you've got a big dream, it
could be around fashion,

00:01:26.518 --> 00:01:28.610
and we love that,

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.289
you get inspired by
Evan, which is brilliant,

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:33.966
but you have got the platform where,

00:01:33.966 --> 00:01:34.942
I hate to use that word,

00:01:34.942 --> 00:01:38.007
but you could kind of moonlight
doing your current job

00:01:38.007 --> 00:01:40.815
where you get an income
from being a social worker,

00:01:40.815 --> 00:01:44.332
but use that, and use the
time at weekends and evenings

00:01:44.332 --> 00:01:47.101
to start creating your big idea.

00:01:47.101 --> 00:01:49.282
And you're probably
going to have a website

00:01:49.282 --> 00:01:53.482
associated with that products, and design,

00:01:53.482 --> 00:01:57.101
and maybe even start talking
to potential customers

00:01:57.101 --> 00:02:00.185
and potential sort of
distributors and stuff life that,

00:02:00.185 --> 00:02:02.868
and even a potential manufacturer.

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:05.455
So what would be a
really cool idea, right,

00:02:05.455 --> 00:02:06.989
this would be it Kathleen,

00:02:06.989 --> 00:02:08.882
and you got to promise you can do this,

00:02:08.882 --> 00:02:11.488
we're going to do another of
these broadcasts in a year's time,

00:02:11.488 --> 00:02:14.152
and you're going to come
on the channel and say,

00:02:14.152 --> 00:02:18.377
"Evan, I'm now running a
designer fashion business

00:02:18.377 --> 00:02:20.434
"with a million dollar turnover,

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:23.609
"and I did it because of that broadcast

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:25.583
"gave me the inspiration.

00:02:25.583 --> 00:02:28.946
"And I spent six months
still being a social worker,

00:02:28.946 --> 00:02:31.680
"but actually that gave
me the platform to build,"

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.021
even it's a few hundred thousand dollars,

00:02:34.021 --> 00:02:37.190
that would be unbelievable
and totally amazing.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:39.940
So I'd say with all these things,

00:02:41.023 --> 00:02:44.088
kind of cut the elephant
down into little chunks.

00:02:44.088 --> 00:02:45.973
You've got a great hopefully secure income

00:02:45.973 --> 00:02:47.495
being a social worker.

00:02:47.495 --> 00:02:48.611
Use that as a platform.

00:02:48.611 --> 00:02:50.604
You're doing an amazing
job as a social worker.

00:02:50.604 --> 00:02:53.577
Do some moonlighting in the
evenings and weekends to say,

00:02:53.577 --> 00:02:55.190
"How am I going to use this platform

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:57.613
"to connect me with my dreams, my passion,

00:02:57.613 --> 00:02:59.220
"which is all about fashion?"

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.306
and then build that business.

00:03:01.306 --> 00:03:04.355
Go after it, build the business.

00:03:04.355 --> 00:03:08.537
Fund it sensibly just
to kind of kick it off,

00:03:08.537 --> 00:03:10.144
get some product sales,

00:03:10.144 --> 00:03:12.560
then reimburse that in growth,

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.082
and then you'll find you've
got a business you love.

00:03:16.082 --> 00:03:18.194
The only tough decision you've got

00:03:18.194 --> 00:03:20.119
is when you stop being the social worker

00:03:20.119 --> 00:03:21.946
and give your notice really,

00:03:21.946 --> 00:03:24.191
and I would advocate

00:03:24.191 --> 00:03:26.470
that you kind of jump off the diving board

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.356
once you've got your
business in a bit of momentum

00:03:28.356 --> 00:03:31.706
and you believe in it, then you should go.

00:03:31.706 --> 00:03:32.974
Now the other thing, right,

00:03:32.974 --> 00:03:36.017
I got this great piece
of advice from someone,

00:03:36.017 --> 00:03:37.455
oh wow, when I went off to,

00:03:37.455 --> 00:03:38.911
it was a start up company at the time,

00:03:38.911 --> 00:03:41.308
it was a company called
Oracle Technology Company.

00:03:41.308 --> 00:03:44.975
Everybody knows 'em, but at
the time nobody knew 'em.

00:03:44.975 --> 00:03:47.612
They were a no name company
and they were a startup.

00:03:47.612 --> 00:03:49.812
And I was with a pretty
safe company at the time

00:03:49.812 --> 00:03:51.137
and I went to my boss and said,

00:03:51.137 --> 00:03:53.860
"Look, I got this offer from Oracle.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:56.533
"They sound like a pretty
crazy American company,

00:03:56.533 --> 00:03:58.600
"going to rule the world, big vision.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:02.155
"They got this guy Larry
Ellison running 'em."

00:04:02.155 --> 00:04:04.406
And I said, "I really am torn,

00:04:04.406 --> 00:04:06.954
"because I've got a great
career here, pretty safe,

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:10.953
"but I think I would want to
risk an early stage company."

00:04:10.953 --> 00:04:12.609
And he said, "The good thing is, Steven,"

00:04:12.609 --> 00:04:15.491
he said, "If you leave and resign,

00:04:15.491 --> 00:04:17.430
"you know the door is always open

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:20.191
"if you leave well and you
never burn your bridges,

00:04:20.191 --> 00:04:23.845
"so actually there should be
no fear about your decision,

00:04:23.845 --> 00:04:26.842
"because you're well
liked, you're trusted,

00:04:26.842 --> 00:04:29.224
"you do a great job for us,

00:04:29.224 --> 00:04:31.832
"but most of all you
should go and try that,

00:04:31.832 --> 00:04:33.416
"and if it works out,

00:04:33.416 --> 00:04:36.375
"you're going to be a
rainmaker somewhere else,

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:37.833
"but if it didn't work out,

00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:41.040
"the door is always open here,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.293
"and the only thing that
you might have to swallow

00:04:44.293 --> 00:04:45.326
"is your pride.

00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:46.598
"But you're a big guy.

00:04:46.598 --> 00:04:47.752
"You're a grown up.

00:04:47.752 --> 00:04:49.793
"That will be no problem for you."

00:04:49.793 --> 00:04:50.751
Good advice.

00:04:50.751 --> 00:04:54.950
So Kathleen, I'd love 2017 to be the year

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:58.034
where you make it happen
and you follow your dreams,

00:04:58.034 --> 00:05:00.534
and you're an incredible brand

00:05:02.319 --> 00:05:03.665
in terms of design and fashion.

00:05:03.665 --> 00:05:05.623
That would be amazing.

00:05:05.623 --> 00:05:09.484
- I like the one year
challenge to get to a million.

00:05:09.484 --> 00:05:10.317
I love that.

00:05:10.317 --> 00:05:13.415
And what did you say about
elephant, cutting it into chunks?

00:05:13.415 --> 00:05:14.248
What was that expression?

00:05:14.248 --> 00:05:16.443
- Yeah, yeah, yeah,
hey, oh, they say this.

00:05:16.443 --> 00:05:18.481
Like they say, "Let's bring
the moose in the room,"

00:05:18.481 --> 00:05:19.474
in Canada.

00:05:19.474 --> 00:05:21.213
We say over in Europe,

00:05:21.213 --> 00:05:22.985
"Let's get the elephant on the table."

00:05:22.985 --> 00:05:24.628
But how do you eat an elephant?

00:05:24.628 --> 00:05:27.372
You cut it into very small chunks,

00:05:27.372 --> 00:05:29.866
break it into 2,000 chunks.

00:05:29.866 --> 00:05:32.183
So when you're putting a
business plan together,

00:05:32.183 --> 00:05:33.363
and you're going to be the biggest

00:05:33.363 --> 00:05:37.258
designer fashion brand
on the planet, Kathleen,

00:05:37.258 --> 00:05:38.922
you've got to break it into little chunks.

00:05:38.922 --> 00:05:42.468
What do I want to do
for 90 days, 180 days?

00:05:42.468 --> 00:05:44.534
And then you'll find momentum.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:45.871
You'll find you have a following.

00:05:45.871 --> 00:05:49.448
You'll find you'll have
raving fanatics as customers.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:50.887
And you'll develop partners,

00:05:50.887 --> 00:05:52.696
and hopefully all your employees

00:05:52.696 --> 00:05:55.278
will be big brand ambassadors for you,

00:05:55.278 --> 00:05:58.104
and then you got rolling
thunder, you got momentum,

00:05:58.104 --> 00:06:00.837
but you have to kind of start small,

00:06:00.837 --> 00:06:03.511
have a massive dream, big dream,

00:06:03.511 --> 00:06:05.435
and just a phrase I use, yeah,

00:06:05.435 --> 00:06:07.440
cut the elephant up in 1,000 chunks,

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.751
and then you can eat it and enjoy it.

00:06:09.751 --> 00:06:11.806
- Eat the elephant one chunk at a time.

00:06:11.806 --> 00:06:12.853
Alright, I like that.
- That's it.

00:06:12.853 --> 00:06:15.597
I love it.
- I like that.

00:06:15.597 --> 00:06:18.197
For people who are part time
trying to move full time,

00:06:18.197 --> 00:06:19.337
I agree with Steven.

00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:21.021
I would say you need to make sure

00:06:21.021 --> 00:06:24.299
that you are spending time
every day on your business.

00:06:24.299 --> 00:06:27.200
It's easy to get caught up in
your job and responsibilities,

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.477
and if you have kids,

00:06:28.477 --> 00:06:29.868
life can get in the way

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:30.912
and then you never actually
got to do the thing

00:06:30.912 --> 00:06:33.032
that is also supposedly important to you,

00:06:33.032 --> 00:06:34.033
which is your business,

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:36.470
so make sure you're spending
time on it every single day,

00:06:36.470 --> 00:06:37.581
even if it's half an hour,

00:06:37.581 --> 00:06:41.743
like every day, something
to help your business grow.

00:06:41.743 --> 00:06:43.498
And then try to figure out

00:06:43.498 --> 00:06:45.640
where your skills are best used.

00:06:45.640 --> 00:06:48.548
What's the highest value
that Kathleen can bring?

00:06:48.548 --> 00:06:50.512
'Cause people will throw all
sorts of ideas at you, like,

00:06:50.512 --> 00:06:51.949
"Kathleen, you got to get on YouTube!

00:06:51.949 --> 00:06:53.573
"Kathleen, you got to be on Instagram!

00:06:53.573 --> 00:06:55.848
"Kathleen, you got to
talk to this manufacturer!

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:58.974
"Kathleen, you got to go
to these presentations!"

00:06:58.974 --> 00:06:59.807
whatever it is,

00:06:59.807 --> 00:07:02.732
and you end up doing
everything in a mediocre way,

00:07:02.732 --> 00:07:05.929
instead of one thing really, really right.

00:07:05.929 --> 00:07:08.159
What's the highest use of Kathleen's time

00:07:08.159 --> 00:07:10.163
that you can apply in those

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:12.941
30 to 60 to 90 to 120 minutes a day

00:07:12.941 --> 00:07:14.743
to really make them count?

00:07:14.743 --> 00:07:16.340
You figure that out, and
then you're on your way

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:20.917
to going from part time
to full time and beyond.

00:07:20.917 --> 00:07:22.490
- Hey Kathleen, by the way,

00:07:22.490 --> 00:07:26.378
Evan and I, we're pretty humble guys.

00:07:26.378 --> 00:07:29.227
We're really happy to
do product placements

00:07:29.227 --> 00:07:30.816
for really cool designer clothes

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:33.989
that you're going to create
over the next year or so.

00:07:33.989 --> 00:07:37.811
So it would be pretty cool
to come on Evan's (mumbles),

00:07:37.811 --> 00:07:42.441
and I guess Evan would love
to wear a Blue Jay shirt

00:07:42.441 --> 00:07:45.468
or designer clothes created

00:07:45.468 --> 00:07:49.635
and brilliantly inspired
and nurtured by Kathleen.

00:07:51.226 --> 00:07:53.857
So we'll do product placements
for you, and we'll pump...

00:07:53.857 --> 00:07:54.762
And the other thing, actually,

00:07:54.762 --> 00:07:58.306
if you get going and
you follow your dreams,

00:07:58.306 --> 00:08:00.453
what I love doing is pumping out

00:08:00.453 --> 00:08:03.192
great ideas on social media,

00:08:03.192 --> 00:08:06.511
so we'll give you all the help we can.

00:08:06.511 --> 00:08:08.594
(swoosh)

